#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py:132
#, draft
msgid ""
"Yes: a person may have a picture of the whole page kept, sent by their browser extension or drawn here from the kept source with scripts and the network off. A picture taken in somebody's browser shows the page as they were seeing it, signed in or not. No, or not set: nobody's captures keep one."
msgstr ""
"Tá: féadann duine pictiúr den leathanach iomlán a choinneáil, seolta ag a bhreiseán brabhsálaí nó tarraingthe anseo ón bhfoinse a coinníodh, le scripteanna agus an líonra as. Taispeánann pictiúr a tógadh i mbrabhsálaí duine éigin an leathanach mar a bhíothas á fheiceáil, sínithe isteach nó nach ea. Níl, nó gan socrú: ní choinníonn gabhálacha aon duine ceann."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py:123
#, draft
msgid ""
"Yes: a person may have the page's source kept beside what was read from it, exactly as it was parsed, so that a capture can be checked against it and read again by a better parser. It is kept as text and never shown as a page. No, or not set: nobody's captures keep it, whatever they have chosen."
msgstr ""
"Tá: féadann duine foinse an leathanaigh a choinneáil lena thaobh an méid a léadh uaidh, go díreach mar a parsáladh í, ionas gur féidir gabháil a sheiceáil ina coinne agus a léamh arís le parsálaí níos fearr. Coinnítear mar théacs í agus ní thaispeántar riamh mar leathanach. Níl, nó gan socrú: ní choinníonn gabhálacha aon duine í, is cuma cad a roghnaigh siad."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py:70
#, draft
msgid ""
"Yes: anyone who finds the address may create an account. No: invitation only. An empty instance always offers the sign-up form, so somebody can become the first account."
msgstr ""
"Tá: is féidir le haon duine a aimsíonn an seoladh cuntas a chruthú. Níl: le cuireadh amháin. Tairgeann ásc folamh an fhoirm chlárúcháin i gcónaí, ionas gur féidir le duine éigin a bheith ina chéad chuntas."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py:79
#, draft
msgid ""
"Yes: somebody who arrives through the identity provider is signed straight in, without being asked for a code as well. Say yes only if you know that provider checks identity at least as carefully as Postulo would. It never applies to a password sign-in, and it removes nobody's authenticator app. A passkey already counts on its own and needs no setting."
msgstr ""
"Tá: síníonn duine a thagann tríd an soláthraí céannachta isteach go díreach, gan cód a iarraidh air freisin. Ná habair tá ach amháin má tá a fhios agat go seiceálann an soláthraí sin céannacht ar a laghad chomh cúramach agus a dhéanfadh Postulo. Ní bhaineann sé riamh le síniú isteach le focal faire agus ní bhaineann sé aip fhíordheimhnithe ó dhuine ar bith. Áirítear eochair rochtana léi féin cheana agus ní gá socrú ar bith."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py:90
#, draft
msgid ""
"Yes: somebody who has forgotten their password can ask for a code at their primary address and type it back. A code rather than a link, because mail scanners follow links and would spend one before the person read it. It is never a second factor: an authenticator app is still asked for. Offered only while this instance's mail is actually getting through."
msgstr ""
"Tá: is féidir le duine a rinne dearmad ar a phasfhocal cód a iarraidh ar a phríomhsheoladh agus é a chlóscríobh ar ais. Cód seachas nasc, mar leanann scanóirí poist naisc agus chaithfidís é sula léifeadh an duine é. Ní dara fachtóir é riamh: iarrtar an aip fhíordheimhnithe fós. Ní thairgtear é ach fad a bhíonn post an áis seo ag teacht i ndáiríre."

